{"kind":"report","text":"CE-1 report (request af141d9b, promise 76693645). All five U4-B console errors have one cause. It is expected and is neither a page fault nor a dap platform fault.\n\nMethod: the kept U4-B profile reopened both upgraded screens read-only (no click, no fill), with 20 s on each page. The run recorded every console error and warning with its source, page errors, failed responses and aborted requests. Evidence: artroom-evidence/2026-11-18-ce1-console (report.json b55d140b, page-1.png 851b6f83, page-2.png 4aadd2af). No invitation or token appears in it.\n\nFinding: each page load logs exactly one console error, at index.html:0:0:\n\"Loading the script 'https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/…' violates the following Content Security Policy directive: \"script-src 'self'\" … The action has been blocked.\"\n- Counter 0.7.0 (counter-upgrade.inguz.space): 1 error. Lending 0.6.0 (lending-shelf.inguz.space): 1 error.\n- This matches U4-B exactly: run 1 loaded 2 pages (2 errors), the settle run 1 page (1), and the after run 2 pages (2).\n- Source: the Cloudflare edge injects a `\u003cscript type=\"module\" src=\"https://static.cloudflareinsights.com/beacon.min.js/…\" data-cf-beacon=…\u003e` tag into the HTML that a browser receives. A browser-like curl of the Counter index.html shows it after `./counter.js`. The repository has no beacon: git grep for cloudflareinsights and beacon in apps, examples and packages finds nothing. The screen's own CSP (`default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; …`) blocks it, as it should. The page loses nothing.\n- There were no page errors and no response at status 400 or above.\n\nAlso observed, not console errors: the Lending page had two requests aborted (net::ERR_ABORTED): GET …/5/\u003cpresentation\u003e/_/context and GET /v1/scopes/sc_g65urfue…. The page rendered joined with the shelf, so I read these as superseded or in-flight fetches when the page closed. They are not faults, and I did not trace them further.\n\nClassification: expected. It is an edge injection that our CSP refuses. No dap head is needed, and the CSP must not widen to admit a third-party script.\n\nThe smallest remedy, if you want clean consoles: the zone owner turns off Web Analytics automatic injection for inguz.space in the Cloudflare dashboard. That is a setting, with no head. An alternative head would have the sandbox send `Cache-Control: no-transform` on screen HTML. I have not verified that this stops the injection, so I do not propose it without a test."}